{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CopilotKit/CopilotKit/pulls/3439","id":3392514304,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJxJfAc7KNakA","html_url":"https://github.com/CopilotKit/CopilotKit/pull/3439","diff_url":"https://github.com/CopilotKit/CopilotKit/pull/3439.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/CopilotKit/CopilotKit/pull/3439.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CopilotKit/CopilotKit/issues/3439","number":3439,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"fix: handle empty tool arguments without crashing","user":{"login":"giulio-leone","id":6887247,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4ODcyNDc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6887247?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/giulio-leone","html_url":"https://github.com/giulio-leone","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/giulio-leone/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/giulio-leone/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/giulio-leone/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/giulio-leone/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/giulio-leone/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/giulio-leone/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/giulio-leone/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/giulio-leone/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/giulio-leone/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Problem\n\nWhen a HITL (Human-in-the-Loop) tool has no parameters, some providers (e.g., Google ADK) send `arguments` as an empty string `\"\"`. `JSON.parse(\"\")` throws `\"Unexpected end of JSON input\"`, crashing the tool execution pipeline with an opaque error instead of executing the tool with empty args.\n\nFixes #3263\n\n## Root Cause\n\nIn `run-handler.ts`, both the specific-tool and wildcard-tool execution paths call `JSON.parse(toolCall.function.arguments)` without checking for empty/falsy values:\n\n```ts\n// Line 309 — specific tool path\nparsedArgs = JSON.parse(toolCall.function.arguments); // crashes on \"\"\n\n// Line 448 — wildcard tool path  \nparsedArgs = JSON.parse(toolCall.function.arguments); // crashes on \"\"\n```\n\n## Fix\n\nTreat empty/falsy argument strings as `{}` (empty object) before parsing:\n\n```ts\nconst rawArgs = toolCall.function.arguments;\nparsedArgs = rawArgs ? JSON.parse(rawArgs) : {};\n```\n\nThis matches the existing defensive patterns:\n- **v1 `agui-to-gql.ts`**: already catches parse errors and falls back to `{}`\n- **v2 `web-inspector`**: already checks `args === \"\"  ` before parsing (line 818)\n\n## Changes\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `packages/v2/core/src/core/run-handler.ts` | Safe empty-args fallback at both parse sites |\n| `packages/v2/core/src/__tests__/core-edge-cases.test.ts` | Updated test: empty args → handler called with `{}` |\n| `packages/v2/core/src/__tests__/core-full.test.ts` | Updated test: empty args → handler called with `{}` |\n\n## Testing\n\n- All 230 passing tests still pass (61 pre-existing failures in unrelated packages unchanged)\n- Updated 2 tests that previously expected a crash on empty args to verify the handler is called with `{}`\n","created_at":"2026-03-13T00:34:51Z","updated_at":"2026-03-13T17:32:24Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"mme","id":247775,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0Nzc3NQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247775?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mme","html_url":"https://github.com/mme","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mme/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mme/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mme/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mme/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mme/subscriptions","organizations_